# CTF02 public postreturn observation source proposal

SOURCE ONLY. This directory is not a frozen engine packet or an actual build/run proof.
The old CTF01 sources, packets and outputs remain immutable. No source formula is
replaced: each helper still executes the unchanged whole public
`ConstructionProps::calculateTransferFunction` method through the same three
CTF01 passive callbacks, then copies actual public members after a real return.

`ctf02_public_fields.hh` is shared by fresh forks of both accepted helpers. The
unit lane preserves the genuine 39 model / 42 operation input rows, including
single and multiple resistive layers; its members remain literal input seeds,
not Material-loader observations. The production lane preserves all ordered 15
original IDFs, 45 inherited guard refs, 13 public lifecycle phases and actual
loader-owned Material/Construct/use/timestep fields. Whole-call counts are
derived from the actual loaded Construct array. No prior observed count is an
expected result.

The public copier reads four complete 19-slot arrays (`CTFOutside`, `CTFCross`,
`CTFInside`, `CTFFlux`), `CTFTimeStep`, `UValue`, `NumHistories`, `NumCTFTerms`,
actual owner identity and caller `TimeStepZone`. It reads no private `s0`, `e`,
`s` or unassigned local. Source selection uses an integrity-valid genuine
PostConversion snapshot and the literal predicate
`!(LayersInConstruct > NumResLayers)`, actual used/no-source/1D members and
preprocessing error state. It is not a claimed Native branch flag.

Every selected return requires all 19 slots, exact count/type/shape/class and
signed-zero sign. The six separate numeric profiles (four arrays, timestep, U)
propose `atol=rtol=0` before new CTF02 observations. Returned massive storage is
retained only as unpaired context. Unused/error/unreached observations never
become zero-valued selected results or PASS. Source exceptions/OS stops retain
their real outcomes without fabricated return snapshots. Public-copy failures
are observer failures, separate from the unchanged source-call outcome. The
helper itself makes no numerical comparison or card/gate certification.

The two JSON files are input/projection proposals, not runnable operand packets.
Fresh CTF02 scope authority, source/request/cases/tolerances/projection/admission
and freeze receipt must exist before either helper executes. Admission requires
the exact shared policy in request/admission/projection/tolerances and the six
zero profiles. Its fresh flag is `frozen_before_this_CTF02_helper_execution`;
inherited CTF01 freezes are historical input authorities, not backdated CTF02
freezes. Actual future refs remain null in this proposal.

Each lane's `native_source_files` contains eight exact source identities: the
new main, new admission, shared new copier, unchanged inherited metadata and
lane fields, and unchanged derived Construction / observer header / observer
implementation. The manifest records their exact paths and bytes. The four
before copies and generated diffs expose all changes to inherited helper code.

Both helpers retain argc5: `<root> <fresh-request> <fresh-admission> <fresh-output>`.
Output is confined to a new directory below `.runtime/porting/CTF-02`.
Unit schemas are `ctf02-helper-cases.v1`, `ctf02-native-admission-contract.v1`,
`ctf02-{source,cases,tolerances}-contract.v1`,
`ctf02-observation-projection.v1`, `ctf02-helper-results.v1`.
Production schemas add `production-` after `ctf02-`.
The result adds `CTF02_public_observation_policy`; each operation adds
`CTF02_public_postreturn`. The exact original callback ledger remains present.

The CMake recipe adds two targets, `ctf02_unit_helper` and
`ctf02_production_helper`, with distinct main / inherited full Construction /
callback object files. It includes the held CTF01 production recipe to retain
existing targets. The genuine cache must retain its existing CTF01 helper and
production source directory variables, and receive `CTF02_SOURCE_DIR` plus the
unchanged `CTF01_OBSERVER_SOURCE_DIR`. Original archive objects are not replaced.
Root must verify actual unchanged prior compile commands, actual added rows,
compiler/ABI/FP flags, existing registered versus physically present objects,
protected bytes, and each real link map (derived provider selected, archive
Construction member absent), then derive/PE-review before an engine call.
These are future actual build duties; no extra execution framework is added.

Authorship: Header authored the inherited CTF01 helper/observer and proposed
CTF02 Rust branch. This source proposal is not independent certification of
those algorithms. Root and another author review the exact held source bytes.
